# Caddy for TWO TeXLoom servers that are both reachable by the public (INSTALL.md, "Moving traffic to
# the primary"). Put this on each machine, with both machines' addresses in DNS for the name. A visitor
# who reaches either one is sent on to whichever server answers 200 on /api/health: the primary (a
# standby, and a server that has stopped itself, answer 503). Nothing in DNS has to change when the
# servers switch over, and no script runs; people wait only for the switch itself (about a minute).
#
# 1. Replace the name below, and PEER with the other machine's relay address.
# 2. The relay must be reachable from the other machine, and ONLY from it: it speaks plain HTTP. Use a
#    private network (WireGuard, Tailscale). The relay listens on one address (`host =` in texloom.toml):
#    either bind it to this machine's private address and use that address instead of 127.0.0.1 below, or
#    bind it to 0.0.0.0 and firewall port 8787 so that only the other machine can reach it. Never open
#    8787 to the internet.
# 3. Certificates: both machines answer for the same name, so a certificate request from one can be
#    validated against the other and fail. Use the DNS challenge on both (a Caddy build with your DNS
#    provider's module), or share Caddy's storage between them (Caddy's documentation on clustering).
#    Not tried here.
# 4. sudo caddy run --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#
# Each Caddy sets X-Real-IP to the visitor's address before forwarding, so the relay's per-address limits
# see the real visitor whichever machine they reached.
texloom.example.org {
	encode zstd gzip

	@upload path /blob/*
	request_body @upload {
		max_size 75MB
	}
	@other not path /blob/*
	request_body @other {
		max_size 1MB
	}

	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8787 PEER:8787 {
		# the first of these that is healthy: this machine's own, if it is the primary, else the other's
		lb_policy first
		health_uri /api/health
		health_interval 5s
		health_timeout 3s
		health_status 200
		# a request that finds the server just gone is tried on the other for up to this long
		lb_try_duration 20s
		lb_try_interval 1s
		header_up X-Real-IP {remote_host}
	}
}
